lted after us-east: orchestrator error", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 8425, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EXbM2mivv4iCSDXEfRqoYN", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 10716, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LmmeoJPDmRdeJGi7VFBBPW", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 11016, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LmmeoJPDmRdeJGi7VFBBPW", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 11016, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LmmeoJPDmRdeJGi7VFBBPW", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 13727, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01RgojojqJZgE4Jsi1T2efs9", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17727, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RgojojqJZgE4Jsi1T2efs9", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17727, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RgojojqJZgE4Jsi1T2efs9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19585, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01J5S57heoXCfWmUDK4HGeqr", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19885, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01J5S57heoXCfWmUDK4HGeqr", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19885, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01J5S57heoXCfWmUDK4HGeqr", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19885, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01HKCqkC7dnMv9PzUcxfmwC7", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20185, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HKCqkC7dnMv9PzUcxfmwC7", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20185, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HKCqkC7dnMv9PzUcxfmwC7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25149, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WnuJeQ3ezAUHuTxZLsee64", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and look at why a release that was unhealthy in staging still reached production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55749, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WnuJeQ3ezAUHuTxZLsee64", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55749, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WnuJeQ3ezAUHuTxZLsee64", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57380, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WgsDdCHm4CDoU5ADaqS2Si", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57680, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WgsDdCHm4CDoU5ADaqS2Si", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57680, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WgsDdCHm4CDoU5ADaqS2Si", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62872, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. The release-candidate version had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It had been healthy before, so it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished.\n- All three regions now run v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't submit it again. That means only one page went out.\n- **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api) is open. It describes the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n- It lists three follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and look at why a release that was unhealthy in staging still reached production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HtWufDjmGfrDtcfMV5UdvC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Uxr3hXUkXXQWpS9TrA6swv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EXbM2mivv4iCSDXEfRqoYN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LmmeoJPDmRdeJGi7VFBBPW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0 but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same healthy version again doesn't make anything worse, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RgojojqJZgE4Jsi1T2efs9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J5S57heoXCfWmUDK4HGeqr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HKCqkC7dnMv9PzUcxfmwC7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WnuJeQ3ezAUHuTxZLsee64", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and look at why a release that was unhealthy in staging still reached production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01WgsDdCHm4CDoU5ADaqS2Si", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. The release-candidate version had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It had been healthy before, so it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished.\n- All three regions now run v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't submit it again. That means only one page went out.\n- **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api) is open. It describes the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n- It lists three follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and look at why a release that was unhealthy in staging still reached production.", "type": "text"}]}]}